              "originalPosition": 77,
              "body": "It's mostly to avoid too many mentions of `foo - 1` and have 2 distinct terms that can be used plainly. \"Domain separator\" is just a name for that uniqueness input to the hashing. So it's as-is, but just with named inputs rather than -+1 arithmetic.\n\nHowever I agree in hindsight it's a bit overly specific. Will simplify back towards the original",
